      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(12x-{5}^{∘})+(6x+{5}^{∘})+(10x)+(9x-{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 37x-{10}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 37x & ={360}^{∘}+{10}^{∘} \\\\ 37x & ={370}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-{5}^{∘} & =12({10}^{∘})-{5}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}-{5}^{∘} \\\\  & ={115}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
